BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roots of the Valleys: A Photography Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260713T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260713T170000
UID:260708m0LlYC3ZjE25hp99uqJ31w
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center proudly presents: Roo
 ts of the Valleys Photography Exhibition in the Maurice Del Mue Galleries 
 from July 7 - 31.  There will be a reception for the artists on July 12\,
  from 4 - 7 pm. \n\n Roots of the Valleys brings together the work of 20 
 local professional and amateur photographers in a collective exploration o
 f the San Geronimo and Nicasio Valleys. Through images of landscape\, peop
 le\, wildlife\, architecture\, and everyday life\, the exhibition reflects
  the distinctive character\, history\, and sense of place that define thes
 e rural communities. Together\, these diverse perspectives create a visual
  portrait of the valleys and the connections that root us to them.\n\n Ar
 tists Include:\n\nGisela Alvarado\, John Andrew Murphy\, Velvy Appleton\, 
 Marian Cremin\, Cindy Davis\, Donn DeAngelo\, Jerry Draper\, Julie Egger\,
  Martha Elizabeth Ture\, Roberta Floden\, Harlan Floyd\, Sr.\, David Glaub
 inger\, Sasha Gulish\, Amena Hajjar\, Mia Johnson-Martinez\, Sarah Killing
 sworth\, Richard Lang\, David Lee Hoffman\, Avis Licht\, Priscilla Patey\,
  Laura Persson\, Todd Pickering\, Taylor Rechtschaffen\, Juliette Valente
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/roots-of
 -the-valleys-photography-exhibit
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mad Scientist Camp - Sonoma Gymnastics Academy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260713T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260713T143000
UID:260701IEv7yz-zQEu4kTV6K1Isyw
DESCRIPTION:Make the most of summer with award-winning Gymnastics Camps at
  SGA! Keep children’s bodies and brains active with careful guidance fro
 m our trained instructors\, and have some fun\, too. We’ll play in our o
 utdoor inflatable water parks\, eat lunch in the park\, and learn basic gy
 mnastics techniques every day from 8:30 AM - 2:30 PM. Each week has its ow
 n unique theme with specialized crafts\, games\, activities\, and learning
 . Enroll in one week\, a few\, or all ten! Sign up on our site\, email us\
 , or call us to register. Spots are limited.\n\n**\\-This week’s theme i
 s: MAD SCIENTISTS-**\n\n*Get ready for gravity-defying fun at Mad Scientis
 t week. Blending the physics of gymnastics with hands-on science experimen
 ts will keep campers engaged\, active\, and mentally stimulated over the s
 ummer! Explore the physics of new Gymnastics skills\, learn about body bal
 ance on the beam\, and get your hands dirty with real science experiments.
  Get ready to flip into the world of science!*\n\nCamps are best suited fo
 r children ages 4 to 12. All participants must be fully toilet-trained.\n\
 nStudents should wear a t-shirt with elastic waistband shorts/pants\, or a
  leotard. Long hair must be pulled back. No jewelry\, jeans\, dresses\, or
  skirts. Please wear or pack clothing layers for if the weather permits us
  to adventure outside!\n\nPlease pack your child(ren) a PEANUT-FREE lunch\
 , water bottle\, and comfortable shoes. Morning snacks will be provided.
LOCATION:Sonoma Gymnastics Academy
URL:https://sonomagymnasticsacademy.com/camps/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
