BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma's 4th of July Parade & Fireworks Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260714T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260714T220000
UID:2607099zWIdBPedUmlznluljutJg
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Independence Day at Sonoma Plaza with one of the nat
 ion's top-rated Fourth of July festivities. The day begins with a communit
 y parade winding around the historic Plaza\, followed by a family-friendly
  festival featuring food\, drinks\, games\, and activities hosted by local
  nonprofit organizations. Proceeds from the festival support Sonoma's nonp
 rofit community. Throughout the afternoon\, visitors can enjoy the festive
  atmosphere\, community spirit\, and classic holiday traditions in the hea
 rt of Sonoma. As evening approaches\, the celebration culminates with a sp
 ectacular fireworks display over General Vallejo's field\, lighting up the
  night sky in honor of America's independence. This beloved annual event b
 rings residents and visitors together for a full day of patriotic fun\, en
 tertainment\, and community celebration.
LOCATION:Sonoma Plaza
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/sonomas-4th-of-july-parade-fireworks-show
 /
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roots of the Valleys: A Photography Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260714T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260714T170000
UID:260708ecNmDUn1s0ektRWn5tPFDw
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center proudly presents: Roo
 ts of the Valleys Photography Exhibition in the Maurice Del Mue Galleries 
 from July 7 - 31.  There will be a reception for the artists on July 12\,
  from 4 - 7 pm. \n\n Roots of the Valleys brings together the work of 20 
 local professional and amateur photographers in a collective exploration o
 f the San Geronimo and Nicasio Valleys. Through images of landscape\, peop
 le\, wildlife\, architecture\, and everyday life\, the exhibition reflects
  the distinctive character\, history\, and sense of place that define thes
 e rural communities. Together\, these diverse perspectives create a visual
  portrait of the valleys and the connections that root us to them.\n\n Ar
 tists Include:\n\nGisela Alvarado\, John Andrew Murphy\, Velvy Appleton\, 
 Marian Cremin\, Cindy Davis\, Donn DeAngelo\, Jerry Draper\, Julie Egger\,
  Martha Elizabeth Ture\, Roberta Floden\, Harlan Floyd\, Sr.\, David Glaub
 inger\, Sasha Gulish\, Amena Hajjar\, Mia Johnson-Martinez\, Sarah Killing
 sworth\, Richard Lang\, David Lee Hoffman\, Avis Licht\, Priscilla Patey\,
  Laura Persson\, Todd Pickering\, Taylor Rechtschaffen\, Juliette Valente
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/roots-of
 -the-valleys-photography-exhibit
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Salsa - Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260714T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260714T183000
UID:260705ecK5lxJKzEyFRbrQ6wpfDQ
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner salsa class where no experie
 nce or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have fun!\n
 \nGreat for first timers!\n\nNo dance experience required\n\nNon-marking s
 hoes soles\n\nNo partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed environment is perfect f
 or learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyable. In this class 
 you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame for partner-work and
  simple turn patterns. We organize our curriculum so that the movements ar
 e easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals! No experience is ne
 cessary and no partner is required. Drop-in fee is $20.\n\nDate & Time: Tu
 esdays @ 5:30PM – 6:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/beginner-salsa-tuesdays
 /17157360/2026-07-14T17
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260714T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260714T200000
UID:260704RMFcfYOjhE-o12g-tXNhjA
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 7:00 pm – 8:00 PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-class-intermediate-tuesday/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
