BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Molly Tuttle & Sean Watkins
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260716T000000
UID:260702PBQ8Ilj7oU2KCAP7p8WBNA
DESCRIPTION:Molly Tuttle is a multi-Grammy-winning singer\, songwriter\, a
 nd virtuosic guitarist whose innovative blend of bluegrass\, Americana\, p
 op\, and rock has made her one of the most dynamic artists in modern roots
  music. In 2025\, she released her boldest statement yet\, the critically 
 acclaimed So Long Little Miss Sunshine\, nominated for two GRAMMY® Awards
 —Best Americana Album and Best Americana Performance for the lead single
  “That’s Gonna Leave A Mark.” Recorded in Nashville with producer Mi
 ke Joyce \\(Orville Peck\, Miranda Lambert\, Lainey Wilson\\)\, the album 
 marks Tuttle’s fifth full-length release and her most ambitious reinvent
 ion to date: a vibrant\, deeply personal body of work rooted in self-accep
 tance and transformation. \n\nA highly decorated artist\, Tuttle has been 
 nominated for 5 GRAMMY Awards \\(including in the Best New Artist category
 \\) and earned back-to-back GRAMMY wins for Best Bluegrass Album with her 
 band Golden Highway - Crooked Tree \\(2022\\) and City of Gold \\(2023\\) 
 - becoming the first artist in the category’s history to do so. She is a
 lso the first woman to receive the IBMA Guitar Player of the Year award\, 
 alongside multiple additional IBMA and Americana Music Awards.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1038977558?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roots of the Valleys: A Photography Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T170000
UID:260708mYNTy3UD3kSahU-Q4daZ2w
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center proudly presents: Roo
 ts of the Valleys Photography Exhibition in the Maurice Del Mue Galleries 
 from July 7 - 31.  There will be a reception for the artists on July 12\,
  from 4 - 7 pm. \n\n Roots of the Valleys brings together the work of 20 
 local professional and amateur photographers in a collective exploration o
 f the San Geronimo and Nicasio Valleys. Through images of landscape\, peop
 le\, wildlife\, architecture\, and everyday life\, the exhibition reflects
  the distinctive character\, history\, and sense of place that define thes
 e rural communities. Together\, these diverse perspectives create a visual
  portrait of the valleys and the connections that root us to them.\n\n Ar
 tists Include:\n\nGisela Alvarado\, John Andrew Murphy\, Velvy Appleton\, 
 Marian Cremin\, Cindy Davis\, Donn DeAngelo\, Jerry Draper\, Julie Egger\,
  Martha Elizabeth Ture\, Roberta Floden\, Harlan Floyd\, Sr.\, David Glaub
 inger\, Sasha Gulish\, Amena Hajjar\, Mia Johnson-Martinez\, Sarah Killing
 sworth\, Richard Lang\, David Lee Hoffman\, Avis Licht\, Priscilla Patey\,
  Laura Persson\, Todd Pickering\, Taylor Rechtschaffen\, Juliette Valente
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/roots-of
 -the-valleys-photography-exhibit
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Festival Napa Valley Grand Cru Recital: A Night of Pure Brilliance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T220000
UID:260704_rIG3VV_Bk6pZoeB6u7UWQ
DESCRIPTION:Festival Napa Valley Grand Cru Recital: A Night of Pure Brilli
 ance\n\nThe world-renowned violin virtuoso Ray Chen takes center stage. On
  Wednesday\, July 15\, 2026 at 6:30 PM\, the Uptown Theatre Napa at 1530 3
 rd Street becomes the epicenter of musical magic. Two titans of classical 
 music\, Jean-Yves Thibaudet\, the pianist celebrated for more than seventy
  acclaimed recordings and collaborations across film\, fashion\, and art\,
  and Ray Chen\, the electrifying violinist redefining the concert stage in
  the twenty-first century\, unite for their first-ever duo recital at Fest
 ival Napa Valley.\n\nThis evening is not simply a concert. It is a collisi
 on of virtuosity and charisma\, where Thibaudet’s elegance meets Chen’
 s fire\, creating a dialogue between piano and violin that will leave audi
 ences breathless.\n\nPatron Reception at Serge Sorokko Gallery begins at 5
 :30 PM. Guests will enjoy fine wines from John Anthony Family Wines & Spir
 its while surrounded by world-class contemporary art in a stunning new spa
 ce designed by Craig Steely\, located just steps from the Uptown Theatre.\
 n\nStep into the Olivia Decker Power of Music Series\, where music transce
 nds boundaries and ignites the soul.\n\nWhy you cannot miss this performan
 ce:\n\nRay Chen\, a Yehudi Menuhin and Queen Elizabeth Competition winner\
 , Forbes “30 Under 30” honoree\, and co-founder of the revolutionary T
 onic app.\n\nJean-Yves Thibaudet\, a pianist whose artistry spans Gershwin
  to Khachaturian\, with a concert wardrobe designed by Dame Vivienne Westw
 ood.\n\nThe Uptown Theatre\, a restored 1937 art deco jewel in Napa’s So
 -Fi district\, the perfect stage for this unforgettable recital.\n\nTicket
 s are offered on a “Choose Your Price” basis\, making great music acce
 ssible to all. Elevate your experience with a Patron Pass for priority acc
 ess and an immersive Festival Napa Valley journey.\n\nThis evening is more
  than a performance. It is a celebration of artistry\, innovation\, and th
 e cultural heartbeat of Napa. Seats are limited\, anticipation is high\, a
 nd when Thibaudet and Chen take the stage\, history will be made.\n\nTicke
 t Link:\n\nhttps://festivalnapavalley.org/calendar/grand-cru-thibaudet-che
 n/\n\nWURUR239626
LOCATION:Uptown Theatre
URL:https://festivalnapavalley.org/calendar/grand-cru-thibaudet-chen/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Quench at Copia: Route "Sipty-Sip"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T183000
UID:260701LOGI7FSLYk-zdPOxT4460Q
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate America 250 with a fun\, flavor-packed “swirl-abra
 tion” hosted by Master Sommelier Andrea Robinson and special guest Tonya
  Pitts as they take you on a coast-to-coast road trip down Route “Sip
 ty-Sip" to discover and taste the country’s most iconic wines. From t
 he silver screen Sideways movie star Pinot Noir to bold old-vine Zinfand
 els\, you’ll explore the ultimate USA pours perfectly paired with a de
 licious “Taste of The Grove” sampling plate curated by our former CIA
  student and Michelin-starred executive chef. Don’t miss this journey
  through American wine culture!
LOCATION:CIA at Copia
