BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grand Cru Recital Featuring Jean-Yves Thibaudet & Ray Chen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T200000
UID:260630RI7pu0nQ6UqB2j3Ur9qdNg
DESCRIPTION:Jean-Yves Thibaudet and Ray Chen return to Festival Napa Va
 lley for their debut duo recital\, uniting two internationally acclaimed v
 irtuosi. Chen – hailed by the Los Angeles Times as "one of the finest 
 violinists of his generation" – joins Thibaudet\, renowned for his disti
 nctive artistry and wide-ranging repertoire\, in an evening celebrating th
 e expressive power and musical dialogue of violin and piano.
LOCATION:Uptown Theatre Napa
URL:https://festivalnapavalley.org/calendar/grand-cru-thibaudet-chen/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Basic Roadside Bike Repair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T200000
UID:2606302BLmHU3APkKmeWmU-TK5Zg
DESCRIPTION:In this hands-on class we will focus on flat repair and basic 
 bike maintenance. We will also review items for you to consider carrying i
 n your tool kit. As time permits we may delve into more specialized areas
  like chains and cables. BRING YOUR BIKE! This class will focus on tubes
 \, but is suitable for those who ride a tubeless set up. Wear appropriate
  clothing and bring a cloth for wiping grime. You might get a little grea
 sy. Gloves will be available. Limited to 8 students.
LOCATION:Sonoma County Bicycle Coalition office
URL:https://bikesonom.app.neoncrm.com/np/clients/bikesonom/eventList.jsp
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:PRESERVE THE BOUNTY
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T163000
UID:260627WtKbp8nPc0SNHZcJYvNJfQ
DESCRIPTION:Date & Time\n\nWednesday\, July 15\, 2026\n\n2:00 PM – 4:30 
 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nCategory\n\nCulinary Arts\n
 \nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration C
 ost:\n\n$125\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n
 $125\n\nWhat does abundance look like when we meet it with care? Early sum
 mer is when farmers markets and CSA boxes start to overflow — more than 
 any fridge can hold\, more than any one meal can use. This workshop is abo
 ut learning how to respond to that moment with intention. How to slow down
 \, pay attention to what’s at peak\, and turn a surplus of beautiful pro
 duce into something that lasts. Using fresh seasonal vegetables sourced di
 rectly from local farms\, we’ll spend the afternoon working through two 
 preservation techniques that belong in every home kitchen — one ancient 
 and alive\, one fast and endlessly versatile.\n\nHands-on projects\n\nFerm
 ented Tomato Salsa — We’ll build a lacto-fermented salsa using peak-se
 ason tomatoes\, chilies\, garlic\, and a live starter brine that jump-star
 ts fermentation. The result is a salsa with more depth\, more complexity\,
  and more life than anything you can make with heat or acid alone. In two 
 to three days it’s ready to eat. It keeps evolving from there. Vinegar-P
 ickled Mixed Vegetables — We’ll make a crisp\, balanced quick pickle 
 using a house brine ratio you’ll memorize in five minutes and use for th
 e rest of your life. The brine is made with house-crafted vinegar — ros
 é and white wine — and poured over a seasonal mix of cucumbers\, summer
  squash\, and green beans packed with aromatics. These go home ready to ea
 t and keep for weeks. WHILE WE WORK: We’ll graze throughout the afterno
 on on a seasonal vegetable and dip platter alongside pickles and ferments 
 from previous batches — so you can taste exactly where your jars are goi
 ng before they get there. This isn’t a snack. It’s a tasting of the wh
 ole practice.\n\nWhat you leave with\n\nTwo jars of preserved vegetables\,
  ready to finish at home\n\nA fermentation and pickling guide with ratios\
 , timelines\, and troubleshooting\n\nThe recipes made in class\, written t
 o be repeated without looking anything up\n\nEnough understanding of the w
 hy behind each technique to adapt\, improvise\, and make it your own\n\nCo
 nfidence to look at a pile of summer produce and know exactly what to do w
 ith it
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/preserve-the-bounty/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The SpongeBob Musical
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T150000
UID:260617WnzP23iIy0WJClqVshMDdQ
DESCRIPTION:Join the fun this summer with Spreckels Theatre Education Prog
 ram's production of The SpongeBob Musical! Whether your child has never pe
 rformed before\, or they're a seasoned performer\, this educational four w
 eek summer camp is sure to be the right fit. Ending in four Broadway quali
 ty performances that'll surely leave them wanting more!
