BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sunrise Urchin (Uni) Foraging on the Sonoma Coast
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T060000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260715T213000
UID:260707lJzlMphoukuBPmKlv2eO-g
DESCRIPTION:"Save Kelp\, Eat Urchin!" is a sunrise coastal foraging experi
 ence focused on hands-on sea urchin harvesting as part of an effort to hel
 p restore balance to overgrown coastal ecosystems. Participants join a gui
 ded class to learn how to responsibly forage sea urchin\, understand its e
 cological impact on kelp forests\, and safely open and enjoy this delicacy
  known as "uni" in sushi but especially fresh from the source. Guests will
  also learn how human intervention can support climate-impacted marine env
 ironments. Each participant may take home up to 35 sea urchins \\(as much 
 as they can carry\\). The experience blends education\, sustainability\, a
 nd culinary exploration in a unique outdoor setting. Hosted by Fork In The
  Path\, the program offers transformational foraging adventures in Califor
 nia for curious\, nature-minded participants of all ages.
LOCATION:Sonoma Coast
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/sunrise-urchin-uni-foraging-on-the-sonoma
 -coast/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
