SUMMARY:Back pOrchEstra at River Front Cafe. Fridays On The Deck  July 17.
  5:30-8
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260717T200000
UID:260708-R9xNnZOy0qBJ4YRIlxQKQ
DESCRIPTION:Back pOrchEstra!...OUTDOOR show at River Front Cafe. "Fridays 
 On The Deck\,"" July 17\, Fri. Eve.\, 5:30-8:00\n\n224 B Street Petaluma\,
  CA 94952\n\n(707) 347-5147\n\n...Candy Girard\, Gary Potterton\, Tim Esch
 liman\, Luis Rodriguez and Jen Rund... We'll be performing Original and vi
 ntage Roots Rock\, Americana\, Country Blues\, Singer/Songwriter and Weste
 rn Swing with rich acoustic tones...\n\nWe have a single out!: https://orc
 d.co/lxz1l6v "I'm Wild About My Lovin'"\, celebrating the new "Stories In 
 The Heart" album\, listen now!: https://orcd.co/5xga7nr\n\n"...What sets '
 Stories In The Heart' apart is its sense of balance. Resonator guitar\, vi
 olin\, bass\, drums\, percussion\, dobro\, and Telecaster create a flexibl
 e\, roots-forward palette that allows Back Porchestra to move between styl
 es fluidly. The songs echo traditions without reenacting them\, keeping on
 e foot in the past and the other firmly planted in the present." - Vince's
  Hot Picks (Best of 2026) New Releases Now\n\n"The guitars slam like saloo
 n doors\, the violin traces lines that oscillate between melancholy and ju
 bilation\, the rhythm section moves forward with a tranquil groove that ne
 ver rushes but never falters... Back pOrchEstra delivers a luminous\, eart
 hy\, profoundly human record. An album that makes you want to sit on a por
 ch\, watch the sunset\, and let the stories do their work...." - Fred Delf
 orge\, Zicazine (translated from French)\n\nOutdoor dining & dancing event
 ! ...on the ever lovelier River Front Petaluma Turing Basin scene. River F
 ront Cafe sez: "We create our dishes freshly here in our kitchen. Local fa
 rm vegetables and locally raised beef & chicken\, served with fresh bread 
 from a local bakery. Breakfast& Lunch served daily. Mediterranean/ America
 n dishes"\n\nBack pOrchEstra is a compact Shelter-in-Place-inspired musica
 l combo ....going back to the basics... Formed for the first time the lock
 ed-down summer of 2020. The band draws from new original material as well 
 as reworked classics by Hank Williams\, Taj Mahal\, Dan Hicks\, Big Bill B
 roonzy\, Bob Wills\, Bobby Charles ...even Christmas Jug Band tunes\n\n...
  check out the "Dusty Road I'm On" video: https://youtu.be/jj0IIkUyrE4 ...
 a twangy roots rock number with a Cajun flavor and hints of Jesse Ed Davis
  and Sid Page....\n\nThe previous single\, the Neo-Motown/Levon Helm style
  "Ever Think About It\," is here: https://orcd.co/qo5579q\n\nLPs\, CDs\, a
 nd USB-Music Cards available all over\, including https://www.globerecords
 .com\n\nmore at... https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com\n\nBandCamp: https://bac
 kporchestra.bandcamp.com\n\nyouTube: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list
 =PLOTwG2XEiO2O8c0dEI-7hlpI8nr7apiNf\n\nBluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/b
 ackporchestra.bsky.social\n\nReverb Nation: https://www.reverbnation.com/b
 ackporchestra\n\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/BackPorchEstra/\n\nIns
 tagram: https://www.instagram.com/backporchestra/\n\n#rootsrock\n\n#americ
 anrootsmusic\n\n#americanamusic\n\n#rockabillymusic\n\n#twangyguitar\n\n#b
 ackporchestra\n\n#acousticmusic\n\n#adultalbumalternative\n\n#singersongwr
 iter\n\n#folkmusic\n\n#folkrock
LOCATION:River Front Cafe
URL:https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com/shows.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
