DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T170000
UID:260709wvGUYOLKa0G7eu1KORhWbQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 14th annual Northern California yarn lovers ex
 perience from July 17-19\, 2026!\n\nThe Wine Country Yarn Hop consists of 
 5 shops located in the beautiful Wine Country between Petaluma & Ukiah.\n\
 nThe 2026 Yarn Hop is FREE and begins July 17\, 2026 at 10:00am. The Hop i
 s 3 days long\, you can choose to do all 5 shops in one day\, or spread it
  out and hop all weekend.\n\nAll 5 shops are open from 10:00 - 5:00 each d
 ay of the Hop: July 17\, 18 & 19.\n\nYou will receive a passport to be sta
 mped at each shop\, as well as 1 raffle ticket per stop. Participants will
  be entered to win a prize basket at each shop\, AND the Grand Prize baske
 t when a complete passport is turned in. FREE patterns\, and free enamel p
 ins w/ tote or lanyard purchase.\n\nNo need to register - just start hoppi
 ng at any of the 5 shops!\n\nLearn more: winecountryyarnhop.com\n\nPartici
 pating Shops:\n\nFiber Circle Studios- Petaluma\n\nNoma Knits- Sonoma \n\
 nCast Away Yarn Shop- Santa Rosa\n\nPurls of Joy- Healdsburg\n\nPurple Nee
 dle- Ukiah
LOCATION:Cast Away Yarn Shop
URL:https://winecountryyarnhop.com/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Guelaguetza Oaxaca Tierra del Sol
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T210000
UID:260709uzbmGqAILkSpZ9t0jb6VOg
DESCRIPTION:¡Vive la magia y el encanto cultural de Oaxaca!\n\nLa organiz
 ación comunitaria *Oaxaca Tierra del Sol* invita con entusiasmo al festiv
 al Guelaguetza en el condado de Sonoma a festejar el 19 de julio de 2026. 
 En el marco de la gran fiesta familiar\, los asistentes podrán apreciar e
 l mosaico cultural del estado mexicano de Oaxaca.\n\nSerá un día mágico
  mientras se aprecia la sinfonía de la música filarmonica en vivo\, las 
 expresiones dancísticas y poéticas que aluden con fervor los distintos r
 incones de los pueblos de Oaxaca. Se presentarán la mayoría de las obras
  folclóricas más representativas del festival Guelaguetza.\n\nDurante la
  fiesta de hermandad\, se comparten los valores culturales y se muestra el
  rostro espiritual de los pueblos originarios y mestizos de Oaxaca\, Méxi
 co. Los asistentes podrán apreciar las bellas artes ejecutadas por artist
 as comunitarias provenientes de diferentes condados del estado de Californ
 ia. Además\, podrán adquirir algunas artesanías\, degustar de la rica c
 omida oaxaqueña y recabar información pertinente al bienestar comunitari
 o.\n\nEl festival Guelaguetza que se celebra en el Cerro del Fortín en la
  ciudad de Oaxaca\, es la fiesta étnica más grande de América Latina cu
 yas réplicas se extienden a varias ciudades de California y Estados Unido
 s.
LOCATION:Foley Family Community Pavillion
URL:https://www.facebook.com/Guelaguetza-Oaxaca-Tierra-del-Sol-10418787231
 0673
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Etching & Aquatint
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T140000
UID:260709Ez7Bw6tGI0acOdkkMw3NlA
DESCRIPTION:Sundays · 2 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nJuly 12 & July 19\, 2026\
 n\n10:00 AM – 2:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nPrintmaking
 \n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration 
 Cost:\n\n$185\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$40\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$225
 \n\nAquatint and Multi-Plate Registration Join our next two-session worksh
 op and study the art of copper plate etching! Open to new beginners or con
 tinuing students\, this unique course is focused on achieving the rich ton
 es of aquatint and the precision of multi-plate registration. This is your
  opportunity to learn a 500-year-old printmaking process with techniques f
 avored by masters like Rembrandt\, Goya\, Picasso\, and Mary Cassatt. In t
 he first meeting\, you will learn \\(or review\\) how to prepare your copp
 er plate\, design your image\, apply a ground\, and then etch with a spray
  paint aquatint. Between sessions\, your instructor will carefully manage 
 the etching process by immersing your plate in the etchant solution. Durin
 g the second meeting\, you will learn to ink your plate\\(s\\)\, prepare p
 aper\, and operate the printing press. You will also take part in a multi-
 plate registration demonstration to incorporate various colors and layers 
 into a single print. Upon completing this workshop\, you will have the ski
 lls to create beautiful\, hand-pulled prints and take home your etched cop
 per plate\, ready for independent practice during printmaking open studio 
 sessions. This comprehensive course also covers essential knowledge of pap
 ers\, tools\, and inks.  Prior etching and print studio experience is hel
 pful\, but not required. Continuing etching students are welcome to attend
  and continue working on prior etchings or create new plates. Students wil
 l receive instruction\, and can choose to work with the instructor to deve
 lop projects based on their next level of learning. Interested participant
 s are welcomed to contact the instructor for any questions about the works
 hop.  This class requires hand dexterity to maneuver the etching tools. P
 articipants should feel comfortable using tools with sharp edges and using
  printing equipment.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-etching-aqu
 atint/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JAD Experience presents LUNAE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T220000
UID:2607093XmEtEO7k0OLbkjPOhPjcQ
DESCRIPTION:JAD Experience\, the trailblazing series uniting regenerative 
 cuisine and world-class ballet\, announces LUNAE\, its milestone 13th seas
 on. Taking place July 17–19 and July 24–26\, LUNAE is an immersive eve
 ning of farm-to-table dining\, world-class ballet under the stars\, and de
 ep connection with nature.\n\nInspired by the 13 lunar cycles of the year\
 , LUNAE’s choreography evokes the timeless rhythms of creation\, surrend
 er\, and renewal through themes of feminine energy\, light\, and shadow.\n
 \nPerched atop Tara Firma Farms \\(3796 I Street Ext.\, Petaluma\, CA 9495
 2\\) with sweeping pastoral views\, LLUNAE delivers on the original social
  ritual: shared culinary experience at long tables. Following dinner\, an 
 intimate ballet performance unfolds beneath the night sky for just 100 gue
 sts each evening.\n\nEvenings begin with arrival and cocktails from 5:30 t
 o 7 p.m.\, followed by dinner from 7 to 8:30 p.m. The experience continues
  with the ballet performance from 8:45 to 9:30 p.m.\, and the evening conc
 ludes at 10 p.m.\n\nFree parking is available\, and all seating offers exc
 ellent views of the open-air stage. Because evenings in Petaluma can cool 
 quickly\, guests are encouraged to bring warm layers\; blankets and hot ch
 ocolate will also be provided. Guests needing assistance may choose betwee
 n a hayride or a shuttle for accessibility.\n\nRenowned choreographer Juli
 a Adam\, an Ottawa native and former San Francisco Ballet principal dancer
  \\(1988–2002\\)\, has created more than 100 works for companies includi
 ng Houston Ballet and the National Ballet of Canada.\n\nFeatured dancers i
 nclude David O’matz \\(Pittsburgh Ballet Theatre\\)\, Augi Lehner\, Ryan
  Williams\, Saela Rivera-Martinez\, Zoe Lucich \\(Bay Area\, Houston Balle
 t\\)\, Harry Warshaw \\(Ballet Memphis\\)\, Lily Mangiaruga \\(New Orleans
  Ballet Theatre\\)\, Kelsey Mcfalls \\(freelance\, Bay Area\\)\, and Tessa
  Barbour \\(Smuin Ballet\, Bay Area\\).\n\nDinner is led by chefs Brian Le
 itner and Annette Yang of Pearl\, presenting a multi-course menu rooted in
  the farm and its surrounding network. The evening features dishes such as
  beef tartare\, summer succotash\, grilled strip loin\, and seasonal desse
 rts\, alongside substantial vegetarian and vegan offerings.\n\nIngredients
  are sourced transparently from Tara Firma Farms and regional partners\, i
 ncluding Umbel Roots\, Feed Sonoma\, True Grass Farms\, and Holistic Ag. B
 everage pairings include wines from Enkidu and Shokrian\, beers from HenHo
 use and Moonlight Brewing\, and house-made nonalcoholic options.\n\nTara F
 irma Farms\, a working cattle ranch stewarded by JAD co-founder Aaron Luci
 ch\, powers this chef-farmer artistry.\n\nIn an era shaped by screen addic
 tion and fleeting digital distractions\, LUNAE offers a return to genuine 
 human connection through live performance\, communal dining\, and an extra
 ordinary natural setting.\n\n“LUNAE follows thirteen lunar cycles\, with
  each phase shaping the timing and movement of the choreography\,” said 
 Julia Adam\, Co-Founder & Choreographer. “The work draws on feminine ene
 rgy\, expressed through exquisite motion\, repetition\, and release.” \
 n\n“We need to become conscious that we are just a part of the natural s
 ystem\,” said Aaron Lucich\, Co-Founder & Tara Firma Farms Managing Part
 ner. “Land and people heal together. LUNAE's farm-driven feasts at long 
 communal tables\, grown from our regenerative soils\, model this: dining a
 s unity\, ballet as connection\, all under the moon to remind us we're a p
 art of nature's own cycles.”
LOCATION:Tara Firma Farms
URL:https://jadexperience.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BASTILLE DAY with LARA LOUISE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T180000
UID:260706oe1OY8r9XkOfeE1LEEl0vA
DESCRIPTION:LARA LOUISE’s sultry voice has been heard all over the world
 \, her recordings having been streamed over seventy-five million times on 
 Spotify and Youtube. Growing up in Holland\, Lara started out as a folk mu
 sician before making the transition to jazz and bossa nova. She sings most
 ly in English and French\, with an emphasis on French Jazz and the classic
  American songbook from the 30s to the 60s. What better way to celebrate B
 astille Day than with a songstress singing French Jazz?\n\nTogether with p
 roducer and multi-instrumentalist Gawain Mathews\, she has recorded 2 hig
 hly acclaimed jazz albums\, "Alone Together" and "Quiet Nights of Quiet St
 ars".\n\n​​NO COVER CHARGE!
LOCATION:Sonoma Mission Inn
URL:https://www.friendsproductions.net/shows
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Birds & Their Physiology
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T110000
UID:260625IHdPPktEmkKUdEAwK_h5jw
DESCRIPTION:Join Sugarloaf volunteer Steve Callow on this introduct
 ion to bird ID with an emphasis on their physiology. The outing
  begins at the main parking area and heads out Creekside Nature
  Trail and uphill to Hillside Trail. The group will have the o
 ption to complete the Hillside-Meadow loop or go as far as they
 'd like and backtrack to the main lot.\n\nTickets are $10 for g
 eneral audiences\, $5 for students\, youth \\(12-17 year olds mus
 t be accompanied by a parent or legal guardian\\)\, Sugarloaf  
 members\, Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers\, and free for children 8-1
 1. Not recommended for children younger than 8. Tickets day-of o
 n site are $15 and might not be available. Wear comfortable clo
 thing\, appropriate footwear for rocky/slippery trails\, and sun p
 rotection. Bring at least a quart of water\, binoculars/birding g
 uides \\(if you have them\\)\, and if you desire\, a snack. Par
 king fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/birdphysiology26
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
