BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting in Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T170000
UID:260212_koLGatudUq5jze2oWG12w
DESCRIPTION:Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.\n\nOvereaters An
 onymous \\(OA\\) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits.\n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on Sundays
  from 4:00 – 5:00 PM at Christ Church United Methodist\, 1717 Yulupa Ave
 .\, Room \\#4\, Santa Rosa. Contact: Abigail \\(707\\) 293-5888. You may v
 iew all North Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbay
 oa.org/meetings.html .\n\nIn OA\, members experience spiritual\, emotional
 \, and physical recovery by practicing the Twelve Steps and living by thei
 r spiritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is not a diet club or ca
 lorie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of eating.\n\nOA d
 oes not endorse any specific food plan.\n\nIf food is causing problems in 
 your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery is possible\, and
  help is available.\n\nVisit: https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\nFind a meetin
 g: https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Christ Church United Methodist
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma River Upstream High Tide Paddle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T200000
UID:260211aRGXL9KS_0-fiY5J_5WAzA
DESCRIPTION:When the tide is high\, the Petaluma River opens into a quiete
 r\, greener world.\n\nJoin The Floathouse crew at their central downtown d
 ock for a gentle\, guided paddle upstream\, timed to higher tides that all
 ow access beyond the downtown channel and into a tranquil tidal slough. Wi
 th extra water beneath us\, we’re able to glide into calm\, lush stretch
 es of the river that are normally out of reach.\n\nThis unhurried paddle h
 ighlights the natural beauty of the Petaluma River’s brackish\, tidal wa
 terway. Watch for great egrets\, blue herons\, snowy egrets\, turtles bask
 ing along the banks\, and abundant plant life. The calm water and peaceful
  surroundings create a deeply grounding experience—many guests say they 
 feel their stress melt away within minutes.\n\nAlong the way\, knowledgeab
 le guides share stories of the river’s ecology and human history\, offer
 ing insight into how this upper channel has shaped—and continues to shap
 e—Petaluma. It’s a rare opportunity to experience how close wild natur
 e lives to the heart of downtown.\n\nBeginner-friendly. Sit-on-top kayaks 
 and all gear provided.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/petaluma-river-upstream
 -high-tide-paddle/18032819/2026-07-19T18
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
