BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T000000
UID:260604H4pWSP-WeU6-ddDoK51-sA
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Tasting Notes
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108097022?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NextGen Trades Academy Career Fair and Graduation Ceremony
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T203000
UID:260603oP3FP_3EokOUqxxoOh9CgA
DESCRIPTION:The NextGen Trades Academy Graduation celebrates the achieveme
 nts of students completing The LIME Foundation’s NextGen Trades Academy\
 , a workforce development program designed to introduce youth and young ad
 ults to careers in the construction trades.\n\nThe program provides vocati
 onal training\, career exploration\, and life skills development for parti
 cipants ages 16–24. Throughout each cohort\, students are introduced to 
 a wide range of construction-related fields such as electrical\, plumbing\
 , roofing\, solar\, green building\, and general contracting\, along with 
 essential skills including resume writing\, budgeting\, financial literacy
 \, and job interview preparation.\n\nNextGen Trades Academy also connects 
 students with local contractors and industry professionals\, creating path
 ways toward paid apprenticeships and employment opportunities in the skill
 ed trades.\n\nWe are expecting over 110 graduates this year\, marking one 
 of our largest and most impactful cohorts to date.\n\nFamily\, friends\, i
 ndustry partners\, and community supporters come together to celebrate the
 se graduates as they take their next step into employment\, continued educ
 ation\, or advanced training in the trades.\n\nNextGen Graduation highligh
 ts the importance of workforce development\, mentorship\, and expanding op
 portunities for the next generation of skilled professionals.\n\nWe invite
  the community to come celebrate and support our graduates. Tickets are av
 ailable at nextgengrad.com.
LOCATION:Sally Tomatoes
URL:http://www.nextgengrad.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
