BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:July Poetry Salon: Celebrating French Poetry & Music in Downtown S
 anta Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T190000
UID:260710tF9ghvJNLUeZs5rp0UTZ9g
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special July Poetry Salon at Barrel Proof Lounge
  as we celebrate the beauty\, romance\, and artistry of French poetry and 
 music. This free evening brings together acclaimed musicians\, local poets
 \, and lovers of literature for an intimate gathering where language\, cul
 ture\, and creativity take center stage.\n\nHosted by Timothy Williams of 
 Jaxon's Press with special guest Evelyne Whitman\, this month's salon expl
 ores the rich tradition of French poetry through live readings and authent
 ic French music.\n\nThe evening features a performance by SonoTriette\, a 
 celebrated ensemble dedicated to the timeless songs of France\, including:
 \n\nMimi Pirard – Paris-born vocalist whose expressive performances brin
 g the classic French chanson tradition to life. Jan Martinelli – Veteran
  Bay Area bassist and pianist whose versatile musicianship spans jazz\, fo
 lk\, and world music. Robert Lunceford – Accomplished accordionist and c
 o-founder of SonoMusette\, known for recreating the sound and spirit of th
 e cafés of Paris.\n\nFeatured poetry readings by:\n\nKaren FitzGerald Don
 na Emerson Karen Bramblett Pat Nolan Lance Harmening and additional featur
 ed readers.\n\nWhether you're passionate about poetry\, fascinated by Fren
 ch culture\, or simply looking for a unique evening in Downtown Santa Rosa
 \, the Poetry Salon offers a welcoming "listening room" where every word a
 nd every note is meant to be savored.\n\nEvent Details\n\n Thursday\, Jul
 y 30\, 2026  5:00–7:00 PM  Barrel Proof Lounge 501 Mendocino Ave. Down
 town Santa Rosa\, CA\n\nFREE Admission\n\nPerfect for fans of:\n\nPoetry r
 eadings Spoken word French literature French chanson Live acoustic music L
 iterary events in Sonoma County Free things to do in Downtown Santa Rosa\n
 \nCome celebrate poetry\, music\, and the enduring spirit of France with a
 n evening of exceptional performances and inspiring conversation.\n\n21+\n
 \nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for more events in Downtown Sant
 a Rosa.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/july-poetry-salon-celebrating-french-poet
 ry-music-in-downtown-santa-rosa-tickets-1993577461854?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roots of the Valleys: A Photography Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T170000
UID:260708nZ93GUO1lEWxWLcdCJCDdg
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center proudly presents: Roo
 ts of the Valleys Photography Exhibition in the Maurice Del Mue Galleries 
 from July 7 - 31.  There will be a reception for the artists on July 12\,
  from 4 - 7 pm. \n\n Roots of the Valleys brings together the work of 20 
 local professional and amateur photographers in a collective exploration o
 f the San Geronimo and Nicasio Valleys. Through images of landscape\, peop
 le\, wildlife\, architecture\, and everyday life\, the exhibition reflects
  the distinctive character\, history\, and sense of place that define thes
 e rural communities. Together\, these diverse perspectives create a visual
  portrait of the valleys and the connections that root us to them.\n\n Ar
 tists Include:\n\nGisela Alvarado\, John Andrew Murphy\, Velvy Appleton\, 
 Marian Cremin\, Cindy Davis\, Donn DeAngelo\, Jerry Draper\, Julie Egger\,
  Martha Elizabeth Ture\, Roberta Floden\, Harlan Floyd\, Sr.\, David Glaub
 inger\, Sasha Gulish\, Amena Hajjar\, Mia Johnson-Martinez\, Sarah Killing
 sworth\, Richard Lang\, David Lee Hoffman\, Avis Licht\, Priscilla Patey\,
  Laura Persson\, Todd Pickering\, Taylor Rechtschaffen\, Juliette Valente
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/roots-of
 -the-valleys-photography-exhibit
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
