BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Keys to Health\, Peace\, and Freedom - A Presentation by Dr Wi
 ll Tuttle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T150000
UID:2607095Q91LFIOXkesHVq6Cuxuvw
DESCRIPTION:Are you concerned about the quality of food available today?\n
 \nAre you troubled by the high rates of chronic disease in our society?\n\
 nWould you like to understand the hidden roots of the dilemmas we face as 
 individuals and a society\, and to learn new skills for healthier\, more s
 ustainable living?\n\nAre you interested in practical keys to radiant heal
 th?\n\nAuthor of international best-seller\, The World Peace Diet\, as wel
 l as the companion books The World Peace Way and Food for Freedom\, Dr. Wi
 ll Tuttle delivers an inspiring talk about our culture’s food systems an
 d shares his wisdom regarding practical tools to reduce our environmental 
 footprint\, make healthy lifestyle choices\, and improve our relationships
 \, with one another and the world. Dr. Tuttle and his spouse Madeleine wil
 l guide us toward building radiant health\, optimizing our wellness and jo
 y\, and building a positive future for all. DIscover the knowledge for sel
 f-healing\, physically\, socially\, culturally\, psychologically\, and spi
 ritually!\n\nQ & A session and discussion to follow. Don't miss the chance
  to get your signed copies of The World Peace Diet and The World Peace Way
  - books will be for sale with the author available for signing.\n\nDr Wil
 l Tuttle\, visionary educator\, musician\, and author of the international
  best-seller\, The World Peace Diet\, published in 16 languages\, has lect
 ured and performed in over 50 countries. A featured expert in Cowspiracy a
 nd other documentary films\, he’s a recipient of the prestigious Courage
  of Conscience Award. A former Zen monk and Dharma Master in the Zen tradi
 tion\, he is the author of several books and has created 10 much-loved CD 
 albums of original piano music. His inspiring presentations often include 
 his music as well as evocative animal and nature paintings by his spouse\,
  Madeleine\, visionary artist from Switzerland\, who is also a flutist\, W
 aldorf teacher\, organic gardener\, and vegan chef. Visit www.worldpeaced
 iet.com to learn more about their work.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/616129/the-
 keys-to-health-peace-and-freedom-a-presentation-by-dr-will-tuttle
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx-Beginner Hiking for Fitness
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T130000
UID:260701bdehCqS7NUazemh0hj3pmQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us on this fitness program\, where the leaders w
 ill guide you on a series of 8 weekly hikes with the challenge
  increasing each week. Before the first hike\, the leader will 
 discuss proper shoes\, hydration\, incorporating hiking poles\, pro
 per pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for the long rout
 e up Brushy Peaks Trail\, where hikers can enjoy the beautiful 
 vistas.\n\nThe following is a list of possible routes selected fo
 r this hiking series: 1\\) Sat 8/1 - White Barn to Uranus\, 2.1
  miles\, 180 ft elev \\[meet @ white barn\\] 2\\) Sat 8/8 - Me
 adow- Hillside loop\, 3 miles\, 490 ft elev \\[meet @ white bar
 n\\] 3\\) Sat 8/15 - Lake Ralphine & Spring Lake loop\, 4.3 mil
 es\, 420 ft elev \\[meet @ Howarth Park's Boathouse\\] 4\\) Sat 
 8/22- Jack London State Historic Park\, May’s Clearing\, 3.5 mi
 les\, 820 ft elev \\[meet @ upper parking lot\, 2400 London Ran
 ch Road\, Glen Ellen\, CA 95442\\] 5\\) Sat 8/29 - Vista Trail 
 loop\, 3.5 miles\, 830 ft elev \\[meet @ white barn\\] 6\\) Sat
  9/5 – Stern \\+ Waterfall loop\, 2.7 miles\, 750 ft elev \\
 [meet @ main lot\\] 7\\) Sat 9/12 – Sonoma Valley Regional Par
 k & Lake Suttonfield loop\, 4.3\, miles\, 770 ft elev \\[meet a
 t Valley of the Moon Trailhead on Arnold Dr.\\] 8\\) Sat 9/19 
 – Hillside to Neptune picnic table\, 4.4 miles\, 970 ft elev 
 \\[meet @ white barn\\]\n\nPlease note these routes or dates are
  subject to change depending on logistics. Wear appropriate footw
 ear for rocky/slippery trails and layers. Bring at least a quart
  \\(32oz\\) of water\, and if desired\, a snack. The group will
  be limited to 35 participants.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/beghffsummer26
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T143000
UID:260626-mhRNH19h0eEWtb_15bO0w
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the bounty of Quail Hill Vineyard\, Lynmar Estate’
 s Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing invites guests to experience the flavors
  of Sonoma County at their seasonal peak. The elevated four-course menu sh
 owcases ingredients harvested from Lynmar’s organically farmed gardens\,
  orchards\, and olive groves. Each course is individually plated and thoug
 htfully paired with Lynmar’s acclaimed estate-grown Pinot Noirs\, Chardo
 nnays\, and sparkling wines\, creating a journey that is both deeply conne
 cted to Sonoma County and globally inspired. Served in the idyllic setting
  of Quail Hill Vineyard\, the experience is further enhanced by a special 
 tableside visit from Estate Chef David Frakes.\n\nCollectors Lunch Pairing
  Menu Summer 2026:\n\nAdam’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nWarm Organic 
 Popcorn\n\n*White Corn-Kasundi Salt\, Estate Extra-Virgin Olive Oil*\n\nSu
 sanna’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nThai Green Curry & Coconut Soup\n\
 n*Bliss Snap Peas & Heirloom Radish*\n\nYoung Vines Pinot Noir\, 2021\n\nH
 eirloom Potato & Cherry Tomato ‘Croustade’\n\n*Smoked Bacon-Grain Must
 ard Dressing*\n\nSusanna’s Vineyard Pinot Noir\, 2022\n\nRoasted Syrian 
 Seven-Spiced Chicken Breast\n\n*Indonesian Corn Fritter\, Summer Vegetable
  Ragout\, Balado Sauce*\n\nRosé de Blancs Sparkling\, 2021\n\nChilled Van
 illa Burnt Basque Cheesecake\n\n*Raspberry-Rose Syrup\, Black Tea & Licori
 ce-Poached Cherries*\n\n*Brown Butter Nilla Cookie\, Candied Lime*\n\n**Es
 tate Ingredients:**\n\nBay Laurel\, Cherries\, Chives\, Edible Flowers\, L
 emons\, Olive Oil\, Peas\, Potatoes\, Radishes\, Raspberries\, Thyme\, Tom
 atoes\, Zucchini and more!\n\nMenu by Estate Chef David Frakes\n\nReservat
 ions are required. Maximum group size is six guests.
LOCATION:Lynmar Estate 
URL:https://lynmarestate.com/reservation/type/collectors-lunch-pairing/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It's A Grand Night For Singing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260801T210000
UID:260610rIE-KAliN0-2TcRHeHvlgg
DESCRIPTION:Each program features fantastic professional vocalists as well
  as the most promising professional talent of tomorrow. Singers from all o
 ver the San Francisco Bay Area \\(and beyond!\\) perform excerpts from ope
 ra\, musical theatre\, cabaret\, and zarzuela -- a plethora of well-loved 
 musical favorites as well as delightful surprises from the lesser known re
 pertoire. \n\nIT'S A GRAND NIGHT FOR SINGING continues the first Saturday
  of every month at 7pm at the Jarvis Conservatory located at 1711 Main Str
 eet in historic downtown Napa. Tickets are $20 and available at the box of
 fice beginning at 6pm\, with doors opening for General Seating at 6:30pm o
 r you may purchase your tickets early online.
